    "case_id": "569",
    "case_summary": "A previously healthy 22-year-old man, vaccinated with two doses of BNT162B2 approximately five months prior, was brought by emergency medical services after collapsing at home. The patient had no fever, respiratory, gastrointestinal, neurologic, or dermatologic symptoms on presentation or within weeks before presentation. No history of toxic ingestion was suspected.\n\nThe patient was in cardiac arrest upon EMS arrival. After resuscitation and intubation, vital signs were recorded with QTc of 489.\n\nLaboratory Tests:- SARS-CoV-2 nasopharyngeal swab PCR: Ct of 29 (positive: Ct < 34)- SARS-CoV-2 spike protein antibodies: 1.83 × 10⁶ units/L (<800 units/L)- Interleukin-6 (IL-6): 342 pg/mL (0.0–7.0 pg/mL)- C-reactive protein: 409.5 nmol/L (<47.6 nmol/L)- Ferritin: 512.3 pmol/L (49.4–723.5 pmol/L)- High-sensitivity troponin: 34 ng/L (0–19 ng/L)- Magnesium: 0.782 mmol/L (0.658–1.029 mmol/L)- Potassium: 2.9 mmol/L (3.5–5.5 mmol/L)- Alanine aminotransferase: 137 U/L (5–40 U/L)- Aspartate aminotransferase: 166 U/L (10–37 U/L)- Alkaline phosphatase: 134 U/L (25–115 U/L)- Lactic acid: 3.8 mmol/L (0.5–2 mmol/L)- Urine drug screen: negative- Thyroid function: within normal rangeImaging Studies:- Chest radiograph: small left upper lobe infiltrate- Coronary angiography: mild coronary artery disease with LVEF 40%- Cardiac MRI: EF 50%, no signs of infiltrative process, myocarditis, or ischemic changesCardiac Studies:- Right heart catheterization:  * Wedge pressure: 15 mm Hg  * Mean pulmonary artery pressure: 22 mm Hg  * Transpulmonary gradient: 7 mm Hg  * Pulmonary artery saturation: 77%- Echocardiogram: Initial LVEF 18%, improved to 30% several hours later- Genetic screening: negative for mutations predisposing to arrhythmias",
